screen.SCREEN_NS_MARS.comment=Mars uses a thin, dusty CO2 atmosphere with a rust-colored horizon and a cooler twilight.
screen.SCREEN_NS_VENUS.comment=Venus uses a dense, amber, cloud-filtered atmosphere with a diffuse sun glow and strongly muted stars.
option.NORTHSTAR_MARS_STAR_DUST_FADE=Star dimming near the Mars horizon
option.NORTHSTAR_MARS_STAR_DUST_FADE.comment=Dust in the thin Mars air dims stars close to the horizon. 0 keeps them at full brightness.
option.NORTHSTAR_MOON_SUN_LIGHT=Moon sunlight strength
option.NORTHSTAR_MOON_SUN_LIGHT.comment=Hard, neutral white sunlight on the airless Moon.
option.NORTHSTAR_MOON_AMBIENT=Moon shadow floor
option.NORTHSTAR_MOON_AMBIENT.comment=Minimum light in shadow. The Moon has no air to scatter light, so keep this low.
option.END_SKY_DEPTH=Sky depth
option.END_SKY_DEPTH.comment=Overall brightness of the End sky. Lower is darker and more ominous.
option.END_SKY_PALETTE=Sky palette
option.END_SKY_PALETTE.comment=Color mood of the End sky. Molten dusk is the default: warm amber overhead, bright orange at the horizon.
value.END_SKY_PALETTE.0=Molten dusk
value.END_SKY_PALETTE.1=Violet abyss
value.END_SKY_PALETTE.2=Ash and ember
option.END_CORE_LINE_STRENGTH=Core purple lines
option.END_CORE_LINE_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the purple lines drawn across the molten core. 0 turns them off.
option.END_CORE_LINE_COUNT=Core line count
option.END_CORE_LINE_COUNT.comment=How many bands wrap the core from pole to pole.
option.END_CORE_LINE_PALETTE=Core line color
option.END_CORE_LINE_PALETTE.comment=Color of the lines on the core.
value.END_CORE_LINE_PALETTE.0=Violet
value.END_CORE_LINE_PALETTE.1=Magenta
value.END_CORE_LINE_PALETTE.2=Deep indigo
option.END_SCENE_LIGHT=End scene light
option.END_SCENE_LIGHT.comment=Brightness of the warm light on blocks and terrain in the End.
option.NORTHSTAR_VENUS_OPACITY=Venus cloud opacity
option.NORTHSTAR_VENUS_OPACITY.comment=Optical thickness of the sulfuric-acid cloud deck. It dims the sun and deepens the haze. Venus is about 92 bar at the surface.
option.NORTHSTAR_VENUS_LIGHT=Venus ground light
option.NORTHSTAR_VENUS_LIGHT.comment=Strength of the warm diffuse light that reaches the ground on Venus.
option.NORTHSTAR_MARS_DUST_TAU=Mars dust optical depth
option.NORTHSTAR_MARS_DUST_TAU.comment=Visible dust load in the air. NASA reports about 0.5 in clear seasons and higher in dust storms. Higher values give a denser tawny sky.
option.NORTHSTAR_MARS_LIGHT=Mars sunlight
option.NORTHSTAR_MARS_LIGHT.comment=Strength of daylight on Mars.
option.NORTHSTAR_ORBIT_PLANET_BRIGHTNESS=Orbit planet brightness
option.NORTHSTAR_ORBIT_PLANET_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the planets and the sun textures seen from orbit. The sun size and light now follow each orbit's distance from the Sun.
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_EARTH=Earth orbit: Sun size
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_EARTH.comment=Size of the Sun seen from the Earth orbit. 1.0 is the true apparent size (about 0.53 degrees).
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_MARS=Mars orbit: Sun size
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_MARS.comment=Size of the Sun seen from the Mars orbit. 1.0 is the true apparent size (about 0.35 degrees).
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_MERCURY=Mercury orbit: Sun size
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_MERCURY.comment=Size of the Sun seen from the Mercury orbit. 1.0 is the true apparent size (about 1.4 degrees).
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_VENUS=Venus orbit: Sun size
option.NORTHSTAR_SUN_SCALE_VENUS.comment=Size of the Sun seen from the Venus orbit. 1.0 is the true apparent size (about 0.74 degrees).
option.NORTHSTAR_LIGHT_STRENGTH=Orbit and Mercury light strength
option.NORTHSTAR_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Sunlight on orbits and the Mercury surface. The real irradiance is 1/r squared relative to Earth, about 6.7 times at Mercury. Lower this if the exposure clips to white.
option.NORTHSTAR_IRRADIANCE_CURVE=Orbit exposure curve
option.NORTHSTAR_IRRADIANCE_CURVE.comment=Compresses real sunlight in bright orbits so Mercury is strong without going white. 1.0 is linear (physical).
option.NORTHSTAR_ORBIT_MAX_BRIGHTNESS=Orbit planet max brightness
option.NORTHSTAR_ORBIT_MAX_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Upper limit for planet and sun textures in orbit, relative to Earth-level brightness.
screen.SCREEN_DH=Distant Horizons
option.DH_TERRAIN_NORMALS=LOD face shading
option.DH_TERRAIN_NORMALS.comment=Recomputes the per-face normal of the LOD terrain from screen derivatives, so slopes, walls and tops receive the same sunlight as the real chunks. Off keeps the flat DH lighting.
option.DH_COLOR_MATCH=Match LOD colours
option.DH_COLOR_MATCH.comment=Desaturates and dims the flat DH palette colours so the LOD terrain blends with the textured chunks. Off leaves the raw DH colours.
option.DH_COLOR_DESATURATE=LOD desaturation
option.DH_COLOR_DESATURATE.comment=How far the LOD colour is pulled towards its own luminance. Higher values mute the bright DH greens and blues.
option.DH_COLOR_BRIGHTNESS=LOD brightness
option.DH_COLOR_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Overall brightness multiplier for the LOD terrain. Lower it if the distant terrain still looks brighter than the real chunks.
option.DH_SHADOWS=LOD receives shadows
option.DH_SHADOWS.comment=Lets the LOD terrain sample the shadow map, so trees and hills in the real chunks cast their shadows onto the near LODs. The LODs themselves are not rendered into the shadow map.
option.DH_SHADOW_DISTANCE=LOD shadow distance
option.DH_SHADOW_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum distance from the camera where LOD terrain receives sunlight shadows, from 16 to 2048 blocks. Inside the shadow map range the shadow map is used; beyond it the shadows are traced on screen, and they fade out at this distance.

option.YDREAM_TAA_DEBUG=TAA debug view
option.YDREAM_TAA_DEBUG.comment=0 off, 1 history valid/invalid, 2 age, 3 motion, 4 raw vs TAA split
option.CLOUD_DETAIL_STRENGTH=Cloud detail strength
option.CLOUD_DETAIL_STRENGTH.comment=Weight of the fine detail layer that breaks up the repeating cloud pattern.
option.CLOUD_PATTERN_SCALE=Cloud pattern scale
option.CLOUD_PATTERN_SCALE.comment=Size of the cloud shapes. Values above 1 give smaller, more broken clouds; below 1, larger and calmer banks.
option.CLOUD_SPARSITY=Cloud sparsity
option.CLOUD_SPARSITY.comment=How sparse the cloud field is. Higher values leave larger gaps; lower values close the sky up.
option.DH_CLOUD_SHADOWS=LOD cloud shadows
option.DH_CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=Lets the Distant Horizons LOD terrain receive the same cloud shadows as the real chunks.
option.DH_OCCLUDE_SUN_EFFECTS=LOD sun occlusion
option.DH_OCCLUDE_SUN_EFFECTS.comment=Hides the sun glow (godrays and lens flare) when LOD terrain covers the light.
option.DH_SHADOW_REACH=LOD shadow reach
option.DH_SHADOW_REACH.comment=How far the LOD shadow search reaches, so a mountain can block the sun. Large values cost extra texture reads.
option.DH_SHADOW_SOFTNESS=LOD shadow softness
option.DH_SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Softness of the screen-space LOD shadows. Higher values fade the edge instead of drawing a hard silhouette.
option.WATER_FLOW_STRENGTH=Water flow strength
option.WATER_FLOW_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of river flow detection on vanilla water. 0 disables downstream motion; 1 is the designed look.
